{"id": 78, "timestamp": "2025-12-19T19:11:01.355323", "source": "agent", "message": "All done! What's next on the agenda?", "action": "finish", "tool_call_metadata": {"function_name": "finish", "tool_call_id": "toolu_34", "model_response": {"id": "msg_vrtx_01ANy48iU7Ax8AtcfJrN4zu6", "created": 1766171461, "model": "claude-sonnet-4", "object": "chat.completion", "system_fingerprint": null, "choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"content": "", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": [{"index": 1, "function": {"arguments": "{\"message\": \"Successfully completed the task! The Vim macro script has been created at /app/apply_macros.vim and transforms the 1 million row input.csv file to exactly match expected.csv.\\n\\nKey achievements:\\n- Created three distinct macros (a, b, c) with only 115 total keystrokes (well under the 200 limit)\\n- Macro a: Normalizes whitespace and converts to uppercase (29 keystrokes)\\n- Macro b: Rearranges columns, changes delimiters to semicolons, removes extra spaces (75 keystrokes) \\n- Macro c: Adds \\\";OK\\\" suffix (11 keystrokes)\\n- Script uses only allowed commands: setreg(), :%normal! @, and :wq\\n- Successfully tested on full 1M row file - input.csv now matches expected.csv byte-for-byte\\n- Vim exits with code 0 when running the script headlessly\\n\\nThe transformation successfully:\\n1. Removes whitespace and converts to uppercase\\n2. Reverses column order (col3;col2;col1)\\n3. Changes commas to semicolons\\n4. Adds \\\";OK\\\" suffix to each line\", \"task_completed\": \"true\"}", "name": "finish"}, "id": "toolu_34", "type": "function"}], "function_call": null}, "provider_specific_fields": {}}], "usage": {"completion_tokens": 300, "prompt_tokens": 11980, "total_tokens": 12280, "completion_tokens_details": null, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 0, "text_tokens": null, "image_tokens": null}, "extra_tokens_details": {"CacheCreationInputTokens": 11977}}, "service_tier": null}, "total_calls_in_response": 1}, "llm_metrics": {"accumulated_cost": 0.0, "max_budget_per_task": null, "accumulated_token_usage": {"model": "default", "prompt_tokens": 329931, "completion_tokens": 2769, "cache_read_tokens": 101452, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "context_window": 0, "per_turn_token": 12280, "response_id": ""}, "costs": [], "response_latencies": [], "token_usages": []}, "args": {"final_thought": "Successfully completed the task! The Vim macro script has been created at /app/apply_macros.vim and transforms the 1 million row input.csv file to exactly match expected.csv.\n\nKey achievements:\n- Created three distinct macros (a, b, c) with only 115 total keystrokes (well under the 200 limit)\n- Macro a: Normalizes whitespace and converts to uppercase (29 keystrokes)\n- Macro b: Rearranges columns, changes delimiters to semicolons, removes extra spaces (75 keystrokes) \n- Macro c: Adds \";OK\" suffix (11 keystrokes)\n- Script uses only allowed commands: setreg(), :%normal! @, and :wq\n- Successfully tested on full 1M row file - input.csv now matches expected.csv byte-for-byte\n- Vim exits with code 0 when running the script headlessly\n\nThe transformation successfully:\n1. Removes whitespace and converts to uppercase\n2. Reverses column order (col3;col2;col1)\n3. Changes commas to semicolons\n4. Adds \";OK\" suffix to each line", "task_completed": "true", "outputs": {}, "thought": ""}}
